WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.600
A Run to Remember
难忘的一跑

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.210
Thirteen can be a challenging age.
十三岁可能是个充满挑战的年纪。

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:16.340
Not only did I have to adapt to my changing body, but I also had to deal with my parents’ bitter divorce, a new family and the upsetting move from my country home to a crowded suburb.
我不仅得适应自己正在变化的身体，还得面对父母充满怨恨的离婚、一个新的家庭，以及从乡下的家搬到拥挤的郊区这桩让人难过的事。

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:22.450
When we moved, my beloved companion, a small brown pony, had to be sold.
搬家时，我心爱的伙伴——一匹棕色的小马——不得不卖掉了。

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.130
Feeling helpless and alone, I couldn’t eat or sleep, and I cried all of the time.
我觉得无助又孤单，吃不下也睡不着，整天哭个不停。

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.280
I missed my family, my home and my pony.
我想念我的家人、我的家，还有我的小马。

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:38.860
Finally, my father, realizing how much I missed my pony, purchased an old red horse for me at a local market.
最后，父亲意识到我有多想念那匹小马，就在当地的集市上给我买了一匹老红马。

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.820
My horse, Cowboy, was without a doubt the ugliest horse in the world.
我的马叫牛仔，毫无疑问，它是世界上最丑的马。

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.400
He was pigeon-toed and knock-kneed.
它脚尖内八，膝盖外翻。

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.820
But I didn’t care about his faults.
可我并不在乎它的这些缺点。

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.390
I loved him beyond all reason.
我爱它，爱得不讲任何道理。

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:57.200
I joined a riding club and faced rude comments and mean snickers about Cowboy’s looks.
我加入了一个马术俱乐部，却要面对别人对牛仔长相的冷言冷语和刻薄窃笑。

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.640
I never let on how I felt, but deep down inside, my heart was breaking.
我从没流露过自己的感受，可在内心深处，我的心都要碎了。

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.380
The other members rode beautiful registered horses.
其他成员骑的都是漂亮的登记在册的纯种马。

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:12.750
When Cowboy and I entered the events where the horse is judged on appearance, we were quickly out of the game.
牛仔和我参加按马匹外形评分的比赛项目时，很快就被淘汰了。

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:18.290
I finally realized that my only chance to compete would be in the timed-speed events.
我终于意识到，我唯一能参赛的机会就是计时竞速项目。

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:28.010
I chose barrel racing, an event in which a horse and its rider attempt to complete a triangular pattern around three barrels in the fastest time.
我选了绕桶赛，在这个项目里，马和骑手要用最快的时间绕三个桶跑完一个三角形路线。

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:32.470
One girl named Becky rode a big brown horse in the race events.
有个叫贝基的女孩，在竞速项目中骑一匹高大的棕马。

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.880
She always won the blue ribbons.
她总是拿蓝绶带。

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.470
Needless to say, she didn’t feel threatened when I competed against her at the next show.
不用说，下一场比赛我和她同场较量时，她根本没觉得受到威胁。

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:42.370
She didn’t need to.
她也确实没必要。

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.530
I came in next to last.
我得了倒数第二。

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.670
The bitter memory of Becky’s smirks made me determined to beat her.
一想起贝基那得意的笑，我就心里发苦，下定决心要打败她。

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:55.100
For the whole next month, I woke up early every day and rode Cowboy five miles to the arena.
接下来的一整个月，我每天都早早起床，骑着牛仔跑五英里去运动场。

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.730
We practiced for hours in the hot sun and then I would walk Cowboy home.
我们顶着烈日一练就是几个小时，然后我总是牵着牛仔走回家。

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.650
On the way home I would be so tired; those five miles seemed twice as long.
回家的路上我总是累得要命，那五英里似乎有平时的两倍长。

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:09.530
All of our hard work didn’t make me feel confident by the time the show came.
尽管我们这么刻苦地练习，到比赛来临时，我还是没有信心。

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:17.610
I sat at the gate and sweated it out while I watched Becky and her horse charge through the pattern of barrels, finishing the course with ease.
我坐在门口，忐忑地熬着，看着贝基和她的马冲过一个个桶，轻轻松松跑完了全程。

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.810
My turn finally came.
终于轮到我了。

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.930
No cheers filled the air when I finished my show.
我跑完时，场上没有一声欢呼。
